/-!
# The different of a locally quasi-finite syntomic morphism is its Kähler different

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a locally quasi-finite syntomic morphism of locally Noetherian schemes, with
relative dualizing module `ω_{Y/X}` and trace element `τ_{Y/X}`.  Then the different `𝔇_f` of
[Stacks, Tag 0BW4] and the Kähler different of [Stacks, Tag 0BVW] are the same ideal sheaf
on `Y`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Discriminant.noetherDifferent_eq_span_det_of_square_presentation`: the Noether
  different of an algebra presented by `n` equations in `n` variables is generated by the
  determinant of the Jacobian matrix of the presentation.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.noetherDifferent_eq_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_of_square_presentation`
  states that on such an algebra the Noether different and the Kähler different agree.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.annihilator_quotient_span_traceElement_eq_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0BWG]** in the affine case, with the dualizing module and the trace element
  constructed.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker_eq_kaehlerDifferent`: the two ideal sheaves
  of [Stacks, Tag 0BWG] agree.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.different_sections_eq_kaehlerDifferent_ideal`: **[Stacks, Tag 0BWG]**, read
  on affine opens.

## Implementation notes

The proof is the source's.  Part (5) of Tag 0BWE gives around every point of `Y` an affine chart
`V = Spec B` over an affine open `U = Spec A` with a presentation
`B = A[x_1, …, x_n]/(f_1, …, f_n)` by as many relations as variables.  There `ω_{B/A}` is
invertible by Tag 0BWF, so Tag 0BW6 identifies the sections of `𝔇_f` over `V` with the Noether
different of `B` over `A`; and both the Noether different and the Kähler different of such a `B`
are generated by `det(∂f_i/∂x_j)` — the second by Tag 0BVZ in the form
`Stacks.Curves.fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_minorIdeal_jacobian`, which computes the Fitting
ideals of `Ω_{B/A}` from any presentation, and the first by Tag 0BWD applied with `h = 1`, the
localization of `A[x_1, …, x_n]` away from `1` being `A[x_1, …, x_n]` itself.  The transport of the
Noether different along that isomorphism is `Stacks.Discriminant.noetherDifferent_map_of_algEquiv`.

Flatness and finite presentation of `f` are not assumed: the source derives them from
syntomicity, and so do the statements here, through `AlgebraicGeometry.flat` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.locallyOfFinitePresentation`.  The relative dualizing module and the trace
element appear as the data `Stacks.Discriminant.RelativeDualizingModuleData` and
`Stacks.Discriminant.RelativeTraceSection`, which is how the different of Tag 0BW4 is defined;
no hypothesis beyond Tags 0BVG and 0BVJ is involved.

The Kähler different is an `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`, while the different is a
submodule sheaf of `𝒪_Y`; the two are compared through
`AlgebraicGeometry.annihilatorIdeal'` of the cokernel of the trace morphism, whose ideal over
every affine open is the different's ideal of sections there
(`Stacks.Discriminant.ideal_annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker`).  Equality of ideal sheaves follows
from equality over the charts by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top`, and reading it back over an
arbitrary affine open gives the form stated for Tag 0BWG.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BWG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BWG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BW4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BW4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BW6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BW6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BVW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BVW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BVZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BVZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BWD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BWD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BWE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BWE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BWF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BWF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u w

namespace Stacks.Discriminant

/-! ### The Noether and the Kähler different of a square presentation -/

section Ring

variable {A C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]

/-- Ideals with the same image under an isomorphism of algebras agree. -/
private theorem ideal_eq_of_map_eq_of_algEquiv {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (E : C ≃ₐ[A] B) {I J : Ideal C}
    (h : Ideal.map (E : C →+* B) I = Ideal.map (E : C →+* B) J) : I = J := by
  have h1 := congrArg (Ideal.comap (E : C →+* B)) h
  rwa [Ideal.comap_map_of_bijective (E : C →+* B) E.bijective,
    Ideal.comap_map_of_bijective (E : C →+* B) E.bijective] at h1

/-- The Noether different of a quasi-finite algebra presented by `n` equations in `n` variables
is generated by the determinant of the Jacobian matrix of the presentation.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0BWD] (3) for `h = 1`: the localization of `A[x_1, …, x_n]` away from `1` is
`A[x_1, …, x_n]` itself, so the algebra presented by `f_1, …, f_n` is of the shape
`A[x_1, …, x_n, 1/h]/(f_1, …, f_n)` of that lemma. -/
theorem noetherDifferent_eq_span_det_of_square_presentation [Algebra.QuasiFinite A C] {n : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation A C (Fin n) (Fin n)) :
    noetherDifferent A C = Ideal.span {(Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦
      MvPolynomial.aeval P.val (MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.relation i))).det} := by
  classical
  have hH : Submonoid.powers (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ≤
      IsUnit.submonoid (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) := by
    rintro x ⟨k, rfl⟩
    simp
  -- `A[x_1, …, x_n]` is its own localization away from `1`
  let e : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ≃ₐ[A] Localization.Away (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) :=
    (IsLocalization.atUnits (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) (Submonoid.powers 1)
      (S := Localization.Away (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A)) hH).restrictScalars A
  let eS : C ≃ₐ[A] MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range P.relation) :=
    (P.quotientEquiv.restrictScalars A).symm.trans
      (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq A P.span_range_relation_eq_ker.symm)
  have hmap : Ideal.span (Set.range (localizedRelations A n 1 P.relation)) =
      Ideal.map (e : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A →+* Localization.Away (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A))
        (Ideal.span (Set.range P.relation)) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span]
    congr 1
    rw [← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  let E : (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range P.relation)) ≃ₐ[A]
      localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation := Ideal.quotientEquivAlg _ _ e hmap
  let E' : C ≃ₐ[A] localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation := eS.trans E
  -- on polynomials the composite isomorphism is the quotient map
  have hE' : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A, E' (MvPolynomial.aeval P.val p) =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) (localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation) p := by
    intro p
    have hEmk : E (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range P.relation)) p) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A)
          (localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation) p := rfl
    have heS : eS.symm (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range P.relation)) p) =
        MvPolynomial.aeval P.val p := by
      change (((P.quotientEquiv.restrictScalars A).symm.trans
        (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq A P.span_range_relation_eq_ker.symm)).symm
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range P.relation)) p)) = _
      simp [Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq]
    change E (eS (MvPolynomial.aeval P.val p)) = _
    rw [← heS, eS.apply_symm_apply, hEmk]
  have hqf : Algebra.QuasiFinite A (localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation) :=
    (Algebra.QuasiFinite.iff_of_algEquiv E').mp inferInstance
  have hmat : (E' : C →+* localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation).mapMatrix
      (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦ MvPolynomial.aeval P.val
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.relation i))) =
      Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦ algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A)
        (localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation)
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.relation i)) := by
    ext i j
    exact hE' _
  refine ideal_eq_of_map_eq_of_algEquiv E' ?_
  rw [noetherDifferent_map_of_algEquiv E', Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton,
    RingHom.map_det, hmat]
  exact noetherDifferent_localizedCompleteIntersection A n 1 P.relation

/-- The Kähler different of an algebra presented by `n` equations in `n` variables — the zeroth
Fitting ideal of its module of differentials — is generated by the determinant of the Jacobian
matrix of the presentation.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0BVZ], for an arbitrary square presentation rather than for the standard
presentation of a quotient of a polynomial ring. -/
@[sga "1 I 7.2" "more general"]
theorem fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_span_det_of_square_presentation {n : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation A C (Fin n) (Fin n)) :
    letI : Algebra.FinitePresentation A C := P.finitePresentation_of_isFinite
    _root_.fittingIdeal (R := C) (M := Ω[C⁄A]) 0 =
      Ideal.span {(Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦
        MvPolynomial.aeval P.val (MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.relation i))).det} := by
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation A C := P.finitePresentation_of_isFinite
  have hfit := Stacks.Curves.fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_minorIdeal_jacobian P 0
  simp only [Nat.cast_zero, Nat.sub_zero] at hfit
  have hdet : (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦ MvPolynomial.aeval P.val
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv i (P.relation j))).det =
      (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦ MvPolynomial.aeval P.val
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.relation i))).det := by
    rw [show (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦ MvPolynomial.aeval P.val
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv i (P.relation j))) =
      (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin n ↦ MvPolynomial.aeval P.val
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.relation i))).transpose from rfl, Matrix.det_transpose]
  rw [hfit, minorIdeal_eq_span_det, hdet]

/-- On a quasi-finite algebra presented by `n` equations in `n` variables the Noether different
and the Kähler different agree: both are generated by the determinant of the Jacobian matrix of
the presentation. -/
theorem noetherDifferent_eq_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_of_square_presentation
    [Algebra.QuasiFinite A C] {n : ℕ} (P : Algebra.Presentation A C (Fin n) (Fin n)) :
    letI : Algebra.FinitePresentation A C := P.finitePresentation_of_isFinite
    noetherDifferent A C = _root_.fittingIdeal (R := C) (M := Ω[C⁄A]) 0 := by
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation A C := P.finitePresentation_of_isFinite
  rw [noetherDifferent_eq_span_det_of_square_presentation P,
    fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_span_det_of_square_presentation P]

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0BWG]**, the affine case.  Let `A → C` be a quasi-finite flat homomorphism of
Noetherian rings with a presentation `C = A[x_1, …, x_n]/(f_1, …, f_n)` by as many relations as
variables, and let `ω_{C/A}` and `τ_{C/A}` be its relative dualizing module and trace element.
The annihilator of `ω_{C/A}/C·τ_{C/A}`, the cokernel of `τ_{C/A} : C → ω_{C/A}`, is the Kähler
different of `C` over `A`.

The dualizing module is invertible by [Stacks, Tag 0BWF], so the annihilator is the image of
evaluation at the trace element (`Stacks.Discriminant.range_eval_eq_annihilator_quotient_span`),
which is the Noether different by [Stacks, Tag 0BVT]. -/
@[stacks 0BWG "the affine case, with the relative dualizing module and the trace element
constructed rather than assumed: on an algebra presented by `n` equations in `n` variables, the
annihilator of the cokernel of `τ_{C/A} : C → ω_{C/A}` — the different of Tag 0BW4 read on such a
chart — is the Kähler different"]
theorem annihilator_quotient_span_traceElement_eq_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing C] [Module.Flat A C] [Algebra.QuasiFinite A C]
    {n : ℕ} (P : Algebra.Presentation A C (Fin n) (Fin n))
    (F : FiniteOpenFactorization.{u, u, w} A C) :
    letI : Algebra.FinitePresentation A C := P.finitePresentation_of_isFinite
    Module.annihilator C
        (dualizingModule F ⧸ Submodule.span C {dualizingModule.traceElement F}) =
      _root_.fittingIdeal (R := C) (M := Ω[C⁄A]) 0 := by
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation A C := P.finitePresentation_of_isFinite
  have : Module.Invertible C (dualizingModule F) :=
    dualizingModule_invertible_of_squarePresentation P F
  rw [← noetherDifferent_eq_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_of_square_presentation P]
  refine SetLike.coe_injective ?_
  rw [← range_eval_eq_annihilator_quotient_span (dualizingModule.traceElement F)]
  exact (noetherDifferent_eq_range_traceElement F).symm

end Ring

/-! ### The comparison of ideal sheaves -/

section Scheme

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {f : Y ⟶ X} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] in
/-- The ideal of the Kähler different of a morphism locally of finite type over an affine chart
is the Kähler different of the chart algebra, the zeroth Fitting ideal of `Ω_{B/A}`. -/
theorem kaehlerDifferent_ideal_eq_fittingIdeal [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (V : Y.affineOpens) (hVU : V.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :
    letI : Algebra Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Y, V.1) := (f.appLE U V hVU).hom.toAlgebra
    letI := moduleFinite_kaehlerDifferential_appLE f V.2 U.2 hVU
    (kaehlerDifferent f).ideal V =
      _root_.fittingIdeal (R := Γ(Y, V.1)) (M := Ω[Γ(Y, V.1)⁄Γ(X, U.1)]) 0 := by
  let : Algebra Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Y, V.1) := (f.appLE U V hVU).hom.toAlgebra
  have := moduleFinite_kaehlerDifferential_appLE f V.2 U.2 hVU
  have hfin : Module.Finite Γ(Y, V.1) Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials f, V.1) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.finite_sections _ V.2
  rw [kaehlerDifferent_eq_fittingIdeal_relativeDifferentials f,
    AlgebraicGeometry.fittingIdeal_ideal (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials f) 0 V]
  exact fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv (sectionsRelativeDifferentialsEquiv f V.2 U.2 hVU) 0

variable [Flat f] [LocallyQuasiFinite f]

/-- The different `𝔇_f` of [Stacks, Tag 0BW4], read as an ideal sheaf: the annihilator ideal
sheaf of the cokernel of the trace morphism has, over every affine open, the different's ideal of
sections there. -/
theorem ideal_annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker (ω : RelativeDualizingModuleData f)
    (τ : RelativeTraceSection ω) (V : Y.affineOpens) :
    (annihilatorIdeal' (traceCoker ω τ)).ideal V =
      (show Ideal Γ(Y, V.1) from (different ω τ).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1)) := by
  have := isCoherent_traceCoker ω τ
  obtain ⟨hqc, hft⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType_of_isCoherent
      (traceCoker ω τ)
  have := hqc
  have := hft
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.annihilatorIdeal_ideal (traceCoker ω τ) V]
  exact (different_sections_eq_annihilator ω τ V).symm

end Scheme

section Main

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {f : Y ⟶ X} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
  [LocallyQuasiFinite f]

/-- The different of a locally quasi-finite syntomic morphism of locally Noetherian schemes is
its Kähler different, as ideal sheaves on `Y`: the annihilator ideal sheaf of the cokernel of the
trace morphism, which is the different of [Stacks, Tag 0BW4] by
`Stacks.Discriminant.ideal_annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker`, is the zeroth Fitting ideal sheaf of
`Ω_{Y/X}`. -/
theorem annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker_eq_kaehlerDifferent (hf : Syntomic f) :
    letI : Flat f := AlgebraicGeometry.flat hf
    letI : LocallyOfFinitePresentation f := AlgebraicGeometry.locallyOfFinitePresentation hf
    ∀ (ω : RelativeDualizingModuleData f) (τ : RelativeTraceSection ω),
      annihilatorIdeal' (traceCoker ω τ) = kaehlerDifferent f := by
  classical
  let : Flat f := AlgebraicGeometry.flat hf
  let : LocallyOfFinitePresentation f := AlgebraicGeometry.locallyOfFinitePresentation hf
  intro ω τ
  have key : ∀ y : Y, ∃ V : Y.affineOpens, y ∈ V.1 ∧
      (annihilatorIdeal' (traceCoker ω τ)).ideal V = (kaehlerDifferent f).ideal V := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨V, U, hyV, hVU, n, P, -⟩ :=
      hasLocalSquareRelativeGlobalCompleteIntersection_of_locallyQuasiFinite_syntomic
        inferInstance hf y
    refine ⟨V, hyV, ?_⟩
    let : Algebra Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Y, V.1) := (f.appLE U V hVU).hom.toAlgebra
    let : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
    let : IsNoetherianRing Γ(Y, V.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian V
    let : Algebra.QuasiFinite Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Y, V.1) :=
      RingHom.quasiFinite_algebraMap.mp (LocallyQuasiFinite.quasiFinite_appLE U.2 V.2 hVU)
    let : Module.Flat Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Y, V.1) :=
      RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mp (f.flat_appLE U.2 V.2 hVU)
    obtain ⟨F⟩ := nonempty_relativeDualizingChartFactorization f U V hVU
    rw [ideal_annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker ω τ V,
      different_sections_eq_noetherDifferent ω τ U V hVU F
        (dualizingModule_invertible_of_squarePresentation P F),
      noetherDifferent_eq_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_of_square_presentation P,
      kaehlerDifferent_ideal_eq_fittingIdeal U V hVU]
  choose V hyV hVeq using key
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top V ?_ hVeq
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  intro y _
  exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨y, hyV y⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0BWG].** Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a locally quasi-finite syntomic morphism of
locally Noetherian schemes — the equivalent conditions of [Stacks, Tag 0BWE] — with relative
dualizing module `ω_{Y/X}` and trace element `τ_{Y/X}`.  Then the different `𝔇_f` and the Kähler
different of `f` have the same ideal of sections over every affine open of `Y`, that is, they are
the same ideal sheaf. -/
@[stacks 0BWG "the global statement: the different and the Kähler different have the same ideal
of sections over every affine open of `Y`, hence agree as ideal sheaves. The different, an
annihilator subsheaf of `𝒪_Y`, and the Kähler different, an ideal sheaf datum, are compared
through their ideals of sections; the relative dualizing module and the trace element enter as
the data of Tags 0BVG and 0BVJ out of which Tag 0BW4 defines the different."]
theorem different_sections_eq_kaehlerDifferent_ideal (hf : Syntomic f) :
    letI : Flat f := AlgebraicGeometry.flat hf
    letI : LocallyOfFinitePresentation f := AlgebraicGeometry.locallyOfFinitePresentation hf
    ∀ (ω : RelativeDualizingModuleData f) (τ : RelativeTraceSection ω) (V : Y.affineOpens),
      (show Ideal Γ(Y, V.1) from (different ω τ).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1)) =
        (kaehlerDifferent f).ideal V := by
  let : Flat f := AlgebraicGeometry.flat hf
  let : LocallyOfFinitePresentation f := AlgebraicGeometry.locallyOfFinitePresentation hf
  intro ω τ V
  rw [← ideal_annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker ω τ V,
    annihilatorIdeal_traceCoker_eq_kaehlerDifferent hf ω τ]

end Main

end Stacks.Discriminant

end
